/* =========================================================
   MAGIC ITEMS DATA
   Content for the "Magic Items" entry inside the "Items" dropdown in
   the Reference pane -- a sibling of "Equipment" (items-equipment in
   items-data.js), NOT its own top-level dropdown. dm-screen.js
   renders items-data.js's ITEMS_DATA into #itemsContainer as usual,
   then appends this file's single MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA entry into that
   same container right after Equipment, via renderDataDrivenReferenceSections().

   SHAPE: unlike the other *_DATA files, this one is NOT an
   {intro, entries:[...]} wrapper -- it's a single entry object
   ({id, title, html, children}), since it needs to be inserted as
   ONE sibling item next to items-equipment rather than rendered into
   its own container. Use renderDataEntryHtml(MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA)
   directly, not renderDataSection().

   STRUCTURE: grouped by item type, then rarity, then alphabetical
   within each rarity (empty rarity buckets are omitted).

   HOMEBREW SOURCE NOTE -- Potions, Alchemical Items, and about 2/3 of
   Poisons come from a specific named homebrew sourcebook (Piccolo917's
   "Potion Brewing and Ingredient Gathering for DnD 5e", a GM Binder
   supplement -- NOT official Wizards of the Coast content), added at
   Isac's explicit request. All mechanics were paraphrased from that
   PDF (Isac supplied the actual PDF; a couple of GM Binder pages by
   the same author were also cross-checked for poison rarity). Every
   item that matches an official D&D name (Potion of Healing, Potion of
   Invisibility, Assassin's Blood, etc.) is this source's own
   restatement of that official item, not a separate variant -- and
   several of Isac's OWN official-batch entries already exist elsewhere
   (Ammunition, Rings) with zero overlap. See magic-items-progress.md
   for the full duplicate-avoidance notes and what's still outstanding
   from this same source (the "Minor Potions" chapter -- ~40-60 mundane,
   non-mechanical items like skin creams and cold remedies -- was
   deliberately deferred, see progress file).

   STANDING RULE -- items whose bonus/version scales with rarity (e.g.
   "Weapon +1, +2, or +3", "Armor +1, +2, or +3", "Rod of the Pact
   Keeper +1/+2/+3") are ALWAYS split into one separate entry PER
   RARITY TIER, filed in that tier's own bucket -- never a single
   entry spanning multiple rarities. Id pattern for these:
   magic-item-{base-name}-{bonus-number}, e.g. magic-item-ammunition-1.

   STATUS: Ammunition complete (6 entries / 4 real items). Potions
   (51 items) and Alchemical Items (28 items) are new categories, both
   entirely from the homebrew source above -- the "official" DMG/XGE
   Potions batch (from the master checklist) still needs to be added
   on top of these later, checking for duplicates first. Rings complete
   (23 items, official). Poisons complete for this source (47 items:
   14 official + 33 homebrew) -- still need official-checklist
   reconciliation per the master checklist's scope note. Everything
   else -- Armor, Rods, Scrolls, Staves, Wands, Weapons, Wondrous
   Items -- still to come; see magic-items-progress.md.
   ========================================================= */

const MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA = {"id":"items-magic-items","title":"Magic Items","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-items-ammunition","title":"Ammunition","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-items-ammunition-common","title":"Common","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-unbreakable-arrow","title":"Unbreakable Arrow","html":"<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Common</strong></p><p>This magic arrow doesn't snap, splinter, or otherwise get destroyed when it's used, so you can simply retrieve and reuse it after every shot instead of losing it the way ordinary ammunition is sometimes lost. Its one weakness is an antimagic field or similar effect: while inside one, the arrow loses its magic, and it can be broken like an ordinary arrow for as long as it remains there.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-walloping-ammunition","title":"Walloping Ammunition","html":"<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Common</strong></p><p>This piece of magic ammunition is built to stagger a target rather than just wound it. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> hit by it must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 10) or be knocked <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a>, on top of whatever damage the attack itself deals.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-ammunition-uncommon","title":"Uncommon","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-ammunition-1","title":"Ammunition, +1","html":"<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-ammunition-rare","title":"Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-ammunition-2","title":"Ammunition, +2","html":"<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Rare</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-ammunition-very-rare","title":"Very Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-ammunition-3","title":"Ammunition, +3","html":"<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ammunition-of-slaying","title":"Ammunition of Slaying","html":"<p><strong>Weapon (Any Ammunition), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This ammunition is crafted to bring down one particular kind of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a>, either chosen by the DM ahead of time or rolled randomly on the table below. Whenever it deals damage to a creature of that type, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take an extra 6d10 Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. The instant it deals that extra damage, the ammunition burns out and becomes an ordinary, nonmagical piece of gear.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Creature Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–10</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-aberration\">Aberrations</a></td></tr><tr><td>11–15</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a></td></tr><tr><td>16–20</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-celestial\">Celestials</a></td></tr><tr><td>21–25</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a></td></tr><tr><td>26–35</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragons</a></td></tr><tr><td>36–45</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a></td></tr><tr><td>46–50</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoids</a></td></tr><tr><td>51–60</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fey\">Fey</a></td></tr><tr><td>61–70</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiends</a></td></tr><tr><td>71–75</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giants</a></td></tr><tr><td>76–80</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-monstrosity\">Monstrosities</a></td></tr><tr><td>81–85</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-ooze\">Oozes</a></td></tr><tr><td>86–90</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a></td></tr><tr><td>91–00</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (Arrow), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Called an arrow of slaying, this weapon is built to slay one particular kind of creature — as broad as an entire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature-type\">creature type</a> or as narrow as a single named race, chosen by the DM rather than rolled randomly (an arrow of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">dragon</a> slaying and an arrow of blue dragon slaying are both valid, for instance). Whenever it deals damage to a creature matching that type, race, or group, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take an extra 6d10 Piercing <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. Once it deals that extra damage, the arrow becomes an ordinary, nonmagical one. Bolts built the same way exist for crossbows, though the arrow form is by far the most common.</p>"}]}]},{"id":"magic-items-potions","title":"Potions","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-items-potions-common","title":"Common","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-climbing","title":"Potion of Climbing","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a climbing <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed for 1 hour. During that time, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Strength (Athletics) checks you make to climb.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-healing-piccolo","title":"Potion of Healing","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>You regain 2d4+2 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-plantspeak","title":"Potion of Plantspeak","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>This clear, brown liquid turns pale yellow once opened. Drinking it grants you the ability to communicate with <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a> for 5 minutes.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-willowshade-oil","title":"Willowshade Oil","html":"<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Common</strong></p><p>A creature can use its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to apply this dark blue oil to another creature that's been petrified for less than 1 minute, ending the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-petrified\">Petrified</a> condition at the start of what would be that creature's next turn.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-potions-uncommon","title":"Uncommon","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-keoghtom-s-restorative-ointment-piccolo","title":"Keoghtom's Restorative Ointment","html":"<p><strong>Potion (Ointment), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This glass jar holds 3 doses of a thick ointment that smells faintly of aloe. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, one dose can be swallowed or applied to the skin; the creature that receives it regains 2d8+2 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, stops being <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>, and is cured of any disease.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-lesser-potion-of-mana","title":"Lesser Potion of Mana","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Drinking this deeply purple potion lets you regain 2 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 2 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 2 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-oil-of-slipperiness-piccolo","title":"Oil of Slipperiness","html":"<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This oil can coat a Medium or smaller creature and its equipment (one additional vial is needed per size category above Medium). Applying it takes 10 minutes, after which the target gains the effect of a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-freedom-of-movement\">Freedom of Movement</a> spell for 8 hours. Poured on the ground as an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> instead, it covers a 10-foot square with the effect of a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-grease\">Grease</a> spell for 8 hours.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-advantage","title":"Potion of Advantage","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this shimmering, golden potion, you gain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> of your choice that you make within the next hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-animal-friendship-piccolo","title":"Potion of Animal Friendship","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Drinking this muddy potion lets you cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a> (save DC 13) at will for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-fire-breath-piccolo","title":"Potion of Fire Breath","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>After drinking this potion, you can use a Bonus Action to exhale fire at a target within 30 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 4d6 Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. The effect ends after you've exhaled fire three times or after 1 hour, whichever comes first.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-greater-healing-piccolo","title":"Potion of Greater Healing","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You regain 4d4+4 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-maximum-power","title":"Potion of Maximum Power","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>The first time you cast a damage-dealing spell of 4th level or lower within 1 minute of drinking this potion, you can use the highest possible number on each of that spell's damage dice instead of rolling them.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-swimming","title":"Potion of Swimming","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a swimming <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed for 1 hour. During that time, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Strength (Athletics) checks you make to swim.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-potions-rare","title":"Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-elixir-of-health-piccolo","title":"Elixir of Health","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this potion cures any disease and removes the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> conditions.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-liquid-luck","title":"Liquid Luck","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Indistinguishable from water by sight or smell, but tasting and smelling like the drinker's favorite fruit, this potion grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Deception, Insight, and Persuasion checks for 3 hours.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-oil-of-dragon-s-bane","title":"Oil of Dragon's Bane","html":"<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Rare</strong></p><p>This oil can coat a single weapon for 3 uses, or be used to dip up to 3 pieces of ammunition for 1 use each. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragon</a> that takes damage from a weapon or piece of ammunition coated in this oil takes an extra 6d6 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> of the same type from that attack. The oil dries and becomes inert after 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-oil-of-etherealness-piccolo","title":"Oil of Etherealness","html":"<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Rare</strong></p><p>This oil can coat a Medium or smaller creature and its equipment (one additional vial is needed per size category above Medium). Applying it takes 10 minutes, after which the target gains the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-etherealness\">Etherealness</a> spell for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-aqueous-form","title":"Potion of Aqueous Form","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you transform into a pool of water, returning to your true form after 10 minutes or if you're Incapacitated or die. While transformed, you have a swimming Speed of 30 feet, can move over or through other liquids, can enter and occupy another creature's space, can shrink to fit through even Tiny openings, and extinguish any nonmagical flame you enter. You also have Resistance to nonmagical damage and Advantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws, but you can't talk, attack, cast spells, or activate magic items. Anything you're carrying that doesn't meld into your new form (such as armor you're wearing) continues to affect you as normal, but becomes inaccessible.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-clairvoyance-piccolo","title":"Potion of Clairvoyance","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-clairvoyance\">Clairvoyance</a> spell for 10 minutes, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-diminution-piccolo","title":"Potion of Diminution","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the reduce effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a> spell for 1d4 hours, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-gaseous-form-piccolo","title":"Potion of Gaseous Form","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gaseous-form\">Gaseous Form</a> spell for 1 hour, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>, or until you end it early as a Bonus Action.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-piccolo","title":"Potion of Giant Strength","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to a set value for 1 hour, depending on which type of giant provided the fingernail sliver used to brew it — 21 for a Hill giant, 23 for a Frost or Stone giant, 25 for a Fire giant, 27 for a Cloud giant, or 29 for a Storm giant. The potion has no effect if your Strength is already equal to or higher than that value.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-growth-piccolo","title":"Potion of Growth","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the enlarge effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a> spell for 1d4 hours, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-heroism-piccolo","title":"Potion of Heroism","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>For 1 hour after drinking this potion, you gain 10 temporary <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> and are under the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-bless\">Bless</a> spell, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-invulnerability-piccolo","title":"Potion of Invulnerability","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>For 1 minute after you drink this syrupy potion, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to all <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-mana","title":"Potion of Mana","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this vibrant blue and purple potion lets you regain 4 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 4 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 4 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-mind-reading-piccolo","title":"Potion of Mind Reading","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> spell (DC 13 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>) for 10 minutes, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-superior-healing-piccolo","title":"Potion of Superior Healing","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 8d4+8 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-true-dreaming","title":"Potion of True Dreaming","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Drunk before falling asleep, this poison-black liquid shows you, in your dreams, true visions of the past, present, or a possible future involving a creature, location, or object of your choosing. The DM determines the nature and duration of the visions.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-water-breathing-piccolo","title":"Potion of Water Breathing","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>You can breathe underwater for 1 hour after drinking this potion.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-thor-s-might","title":"Thor's Might","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>This churning, deep blue liquid, shot through with white streaks, shakes and quivers in its container. For 1 minute after drinking it, any melee weapon attack you land lets out a thunderous crack, dealing an extra 1d6 Thunder <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. There's no limit to how many times this can trigger within the duration.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-tincture-of-werewolf-s-bane","title":"Tincture of Werewolf's Bane","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature-type\">lycanthrope</a> that drinks this tincture must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 3d10 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and be forced to change into its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> form, if it wasn't already in that form — while in that form, it can't change shape again for 24 hours. On a successful save, it takes only half the damage.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-potions-very-rare","title":"Very Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-oil-of-sharpness-piccolo","title":"Oil of Sharpness","html":"<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This oil can coat one slashing or piercing weapon, or up to 5 pieces of slashing or piercing ammunition. Applying it takes 1 minute. For 1 hour afterward, the coated item is magical and has a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-polymorph-potion","title":"Polymorph Potion","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This almost-clear, pale green potion holds the floating, constantly-morphing projection of a creature. Drinking it lets you cast the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> spell on yourself for 15 minutes, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-continuous-healing","title":"Potion of Continuous Healing","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This murky red potion is highly sought after by soldiers and adventurers alike. After drinking it, you regain 2d10 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> at the start of each of your turns for 1 minute.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-enhanced-reactions","title":"Potion of Enhanced Reactions","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This constantly color-shifting potion grants a +2 bonus to all <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> for 1 minute after you drink it.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-flying-piccolo","title":"Potion of Flying","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a flying <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed for 1 hour, and you can hover. If you're airborne when the effect ends, you fall unless you have some other means of staying aloft.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-invisibility-piccolo","title":"Potion of Invisibility","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This potion's container appears empty but holds liquid. When you drink it, you become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> for 1 hour, along with anything you're wearing or carrying. The effect ends early if you attack or cast a spell.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-legendary-resistance","title":"Potion of Legendary Resistance","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Highly sought after by spellcasters, this ink-black potion grants 2 uses of Legendary Resistance, letting you choose to succeed on a failed <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> instead, once per turn. Any unused charges last until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-longevity-piccolo","title":"Potion of Longevity","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your physical age is reduced by 1d6+6 years, to a minimum of 13 years. Each subsequent time you drink a potion of longevity, there's a cumulative 10 percent chance that it instead ages you by 1d6+6 years.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-possibility","title":"Potion of Possibility","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this clear potion, you gain two Fragments of Possibility, each of which lasts 8 hours or until used. Whenever you make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, or whenever an attack roll targets you, you can expend a fragment to roll an additional d20 and choose which of the d20s to use (if the original roll had <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a>, roll the extra d20 after that's been applied). While you hold one or more fragments from this potion, you can't gain another Fragment of Possibility from any source.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-protection","title":"Potion of Protection","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This steel-grey, murky liquid is flecked with tiny beads of yellow, green, red, blue, purple, white, and black. Drinking it grants immunity to every <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-condition\">condition</a> for 1 hour except <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-grappled\">Grappled</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-unconscious\">Unconscious</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-restoration","title":"Potion of Restoration","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This purple potion, full of floating strands of muscle, blood vessels, and organ matter, causes any of the drinker's destroyed or missing body parts and organs to regrow over the course of a week. The regrowth causes severe itching and occasional rashy pain at the site.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-revival","title":"Potion of Revival","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>An entirely opaque, black potion with a single point of light hanging in its middle, this has no effect on a living creature. Poured down the throat of a creature that died within the last minute, it revives that creature to 1 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Point</a>. It doesn't work on a creature that died of old age, and it can't restore any body part the creature was missing at the time of death.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-speed-piccolo","title":"Potion of Speed","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-haste\">Haste</a> spell for 1 minute, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-supreme-healing-piccolo","title":"Potion of Supreme Healing","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 10d4+20 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-truesight","title":"Potion of Truesight","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this potion grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-truesight\">Truesight</a> out to a range of 120 feet for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-vitality-piccolo","title":"Potion of Vitality","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This potion's crimson liquid pulses with a dull light, calling to mind a heartbeat. Drinking it removes all <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> from you and cures any disease or poison affecting you. For the next 24 hours, you have double the normal number of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Dice</a> to spend during <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-short-rest\">Short Rests</a>, and any Hit Point Die you spend during that time regains the maximum number of hit points possible.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-reincarnation-dust","title":"Reincarnation Dust","html":"<p><strong>Potion (Dust), Very Rare</strong></p><p>When this small pouch of purple dust is sprinkled onto a dead <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> or the remains of one, the dust is absorbed and, if the creature is willing, it returns to life with a new body as though the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-reincarnate\">Reincarnate</a> spell had been cast on the remains.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-superior-potion-of-mana","title":"Superior Potion of Mana","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this vibrant blue and purple potion lets you regain 8 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 8 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 8 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-vampiric-essence","title":"Vampiric Essence","html":"<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This violently sour, vibrant green potion is among the most difficult to brew correctly — small mistakes can turn it into a bitter, poisonous concoction instead. Brewed correctly, for 1 minute after drinking it, a fifth of all Piercing, Slashing, or Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> dealt to you is instead absorbed and used to restore your own <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">hit points</a>.</p>"}]}]},{"id":"magic-items-alchemical-items","title":"Alchemical Items","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-items-alchemical-items-common","title":"Common","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-blasting-powder","title":"Blasting Powder","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This volatile powder comes in a small pouch. Ignited by an open flame or a fuse, it explodes, and each <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> within 5 feet of it must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 3d6 Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. Multiple pouches can be bound together to explode at once — each additional pouch adds 1d6 to the damage (maximum 10d6) and 5 feet to the blast radius (maximum 20 feet).</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-bottled-breath","title":"Bottled Breath","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This bottle holds a breath of elemental air. Inhaling it, you can either exhale it immediately or hold it. Exhaling grants the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a> spell. Holding it means you don't need to breathe for 1 hour, though you can end that benefit early — for example, to speak — without gaining the gust of wind effect.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-fake-blood","title":"Fake Blood","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>Crafted to look, smell, and taste exactly like real blood, this concoction only gives itself away to an Investigation check of 15 or higher, or to any level of identification magic.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-grenade-smoke","title":"Grenade, Smoke","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, this grenade can be thrown up to 60 feet away, or up to 120 feet with a grenade launcher. One round after landing, it fills a 20-foot-radius area with smoke that's Heavily Obscured for 4 rounds in a moderate wind (at least 10 miles per hour), or just 1 round in a strong wind (20 miles per hour or more).</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ink-spell-writing-common","title":"Ink, Spell Writing (Common)","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 1st through 3rd level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-muroosa-balm","title":"Muroosa Balm","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>Made from the muroosa bush, this paste is known to prevent sunburn and resist fire. Spending 1 minute applying a quarter pint of it to your skin grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-pepper-peppers","title":"Pepper Peppers","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This fiery, crunchy snack grants 3 temporary <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when eaten. Each batch produces 6 Pepper Peppers, and they can also be made with a cook's utensils.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-soothing-salve","title":"Soothing Salve","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This sticky, sour-smelling salve is applied to a wound. For 1 hour after it's applied, spending a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Die</a> to recover hit points restores an extra 3 hit points per die spent.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-alchemical-items-uncommon","title":"Uncommon","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-blight-ichor","title":"Blight Ichor","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Distilled from a fungus native to the Blightshore badlands, this bitter, chartreuse liqueur grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Intelligence and Wisdom checks for 1 hour to any creature that drinks it, provided it's neither a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a> nor <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> — though it also carries a Vulnerability to Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> for the same duration. For each dose consumed, the drinker must also succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1d6 hours and suffer the effect of a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-confusion\">Confusion</a> spell for 1 minute. An <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> creature that drinks it instead gains Advantage on all Dexterity checks and immunity to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-brew-of-babel","title":"Brew of Babel","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This baby-blue, highly opaque potion grants the ability to speak and understand — but not read or write — a language of your choice for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-fire-balm","title":"Fire Balm","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Applying a dose of this orange, herbal paste grants a +3 bonus to a single Constitution, Wisdom, or Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> made within the next 14 hours.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-forgetfulness-antidote","title":"Forgetfulness Antidote","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This moss-green liquid is brewed to counteract the Forgetfulness poison. Drinking it immediately ends all effects of that poison.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-greater-antitoxin","title":"Greater Antitoxin","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This murky, pumpkin-orange liquid grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on saving throws against Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> or the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition for 12 hours. During that time, the drinker also takes no damage over time from any poison, and can't be reduced to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> by poison damage.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ink-spell-writing-uncommon","title":"Ink, Spell Writing (Uncommon)","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 4th through 6th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-invisible-ink","title":"Invisible Ink","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is invisible once written, becoming visible only to spells, traits, or items that reveal invisible things, or by applying a mild acid.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-life-s-liquor","title":"Life's Liquor","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This strong pink liquid appears completely clear apart from the image of a red heart floating in its middle, which always seems to face the drinker no matter the angle. Drinking it grants 2d6+2 temporary <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-midnight-oil","title":"Midnight Oil","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When burned in a lantern, this oil sheds Bright Light out to 5 feet and Dim Light for another 5 feet, for 8 hours. A creature that stays within the light it sheds for the full 8 hours gains all the benefits of a Long Rest without needing to sleep, provided it only engages in light activity such as reading, studying, or talking during that time.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-murgaxor-s-elixir-of-life","title":"Murgaxor's Elixir of Life","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Whoever drinks this concoction gains <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on death saving throws for 24 hours.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-pixie-dust","title":"Pixie Dust","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can sprinkle this dust on yourself or another creature within 5 feet. The recipient gains a flying <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> of 30 feet and the ability to hover for 1 minute. If the creature is airborne when the effect ends, it drifts safely to the ground, landing on its feet without taking damage. A packet holds enough dust for one use.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-pomander-of-warding","title":"Pomander of Warding","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Once unwrapped, this ball of aromatic spices and perfumes fills a 15-foot-radius area with a strong scent for 24 hours. Any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-challenge-rating\">challenge rating</a> 2 or lower that enters the area must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be turned, exactly as with a cleric's Turn Undead feature.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-quenching-philter","title":"Quenching Philter","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This blue potion always has 2 ice cubes and 2 slices of lemon floating in it, and stays cool to the touch. Drinking it completely quenches thirst and removes the drinker's need to drink anything for 2 days, making it a favorite treat for travelers crossing arid country.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-soothsalts","title":"Soothsalts","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These crystalline, lozenge-sized doses are consumed orally, leaving a telltale crimson stain around a frequent user's mouth. A dose grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Intelligence checks for 1d4 hours, but for each dose taken, the creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or gain a level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> — an effect that stacks with multiple doses. Soothsalts can fetch up to 150 gp from the right buyer, but are illegal to trade in many places.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-alchemical-items-rare","title":"Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-bottled-rest","title":"Bottled Rest","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This purple potion seems to hold clouds that continuously roll past the upper part of its container. Drinking it restores 3 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Dice</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ink-spell-writing-rare","title":"Ink, Spell Writing (Rare)","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 7th or 8th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-meditative-rest","title":"Meditative Rest","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This vibrant orange liquid holds the vague images of two shapes locked in constant struggle. Drinking it restores 4 Ki Points.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-tea-of-refreshment","title":"Tea of Refreshment","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This warm drink removes one level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> from whoever drinks it.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-thessaltoxin-antidote","title":"Thessaltoxin Antidote","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This potion changes color and texture every time it's looked at. Drinking it ends the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> effect imposed by Thessaltoxin.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-alchemical-items-very-rare","title":"Very Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-ink-spell-writing-very-rare","title":"Ink, Spell Writing (Very Rare)","html":"<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 9th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}]}]},{"id":"magic-items-rings","title":"Rings","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-items-rings-uncommon","title":"Uncommon","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-jumping","title":"Ring of Jumping","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-jump\">Jump</a> from it, but only on yourself, without expending a spell slot.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-mind-shielding","title":"Ring of Mind Shielding","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you're immune to any magic that would let another creature read your thoughts, detect your alignment, or learn whether you're lying, and other creatures can communicate with you telepathically only if you allow it (you can end that welcome with a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>). If you die while wearing the ring, your soul immediately transfers into it, provided the ring isn't already holding one — you can then either linger there or move on to the afterlife. While your soul is in the ring, you can communicate telepathically with anyone wearing it, and that wearer can't block the contact the way a living creature normally could; they can use an action to release your soul if you're willing to go. To bring you back to life this way, someone needs to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-true-resurrection\">True Resurrection</a> targeting your soul while it's in the ring — successfully doing so uses up the ring.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-swimming","title":"Ring of Swimming","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this ring, you have a swimming <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> of 40 feet.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-warmth","title":"Ring of Warmth","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Resistance to Cold <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, and you're comfortable in temperatures as low as −50 degrees Fahrenheit without needing extra protection. Wrap up in heavy clothing on top of that, and you can shrug off cold as extreme as −100 degrees Fahrenheit.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-water-walking","title":"Ring of Water Walking","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this ring, you can stand on and move across any liquid surface — water, lava, acid, and the like — as though it were solid ground.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-rings-rare","title":"Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-animal-influence","title":"Ring of Animal Influence","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong></p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge (Action) to cast one of the following spells: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a>; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fear\">Fear</a>, though it affects only <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a> and uses this ring's own <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a> of 13 rather than your own spellcasting DC; or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-animals\">Speak with Animals</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-evasion","title":"Ring of Evasion","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you fail a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dexterity\">Dexterity</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> while wearing it, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> and expend 1 charge to succeed instead.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-feather-falling","title":"Ring of Feather Falling","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Whenever you fall while wearing this ring, you drift down at a rate of 60 feet per round and take no falling <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> when you land.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-free-action","title":"Ring of Free Action","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a> doesn't cost you extra movement, and magic can neither reduce any of your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speeds</a> nor give you the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a> condition.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-poison-resistance","title":"Ring of Poison Resistance","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have Resistance to Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> while wearing this ring.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-protection","title":"Ring of Protection","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you get a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> and to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-resistance","title":"Ring of Resistance","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong></p><p>You have Resistance to one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-types\">damage type</a> while wearing this ring — Acid, Cold, Fire, Force, Lightning, Necrotic, Poison, Psychic, Radiant, or Thunder — chosen by the DM or determined randomly when the ring is found.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Resistance to one damage type, chosen by the DM or determined randomly when the ring is found.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-spell-storing","title":"Ring of Spell Storing","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring can hold up to 5 levels' worth of prepared <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell\">spells</a> at once. Any creature can cast a spell of 1st through 5th level into the ring by touching it while casting — doing so has no effect beyond storing the spell, using up a share of the ring's capacity equal to the spell's level, and the spell stays there until it's cast from the ring or the ring is emptied. If the ring can't hold a spell being cast into it, that casting fails and is wasted. While wearing the ring, you can cast any spell stored inside it; doing so uses the original caster's spellcasting ability, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack</a> bonus, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a>, not your own, but is otherwise treated as you casting it. When found, this ring already holds 1d6 levels' worth of randomly determined spells chosen by the DM.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-the-ram","title":"Ring of the Ram","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can take an action and expend 1 to 3 of its charges to project a spectral ram's head at a target within 60 feet, making a ranged <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack</a> with a +7 bonus. On a hit, the target takes Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> equal to 2d10 per charge spent, and if it's a creature, it must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be pushed back 5 feet per charge spent, unless it's too large or too firmly anchored to budge. Instead of attacking a creature, you can use this property to strike an object within range without needing an attack roll; doing so grants a +5 bonus to the Strength check needed to break that object for 1 charge spent, +10 for 2 charges, or +20 for 3 charges.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-x-ray-vision","title":"Ring of X-ray Vision","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can speak its command word (action) to see into and through solid matter for 1 minute, out to a range of 30 feet. Matter in that range looks transparent to you and doesn't block light — up to 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or 3 feet of wood or dirt; anything thicker blocks the vision, as does a thin sheet of lead. Using this property three or more times within a 24-hour period leaves you unable to see anything for 1d6 × 10 minutes afterward, as your eyes struggle to recover.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-rings-very-rare","title":"Very Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-regeneration","title":"Ring of Regeneration","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you regain 1d6 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> every 10 minutes, as long as you have at least 1 hit point. If you lose a body part, it grows back over 1d6+1 days, provided you keep at least 1 hit point the entire time.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-shooting-stars","title":"Ring of Shooting Stars","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring in <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkness\">Darkness</a>, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dancing-lights\">Dancing Lights</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-light\">Light</a> from it at will (action). The ring separately has 6 charges for two stronger properties, regaining 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn:</p><ul><li><strong>Faerie Fire.</strong> Expend 1 charge (action) to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-faerie-fire\">Faerie Fire</a> from the ring.</li><li><strong>Ball Lightning.</strong> Expend 2 charges (action) to conjure 1 to 4 spheres of lightning, each about 3 feet across, in unoccupied spaces you can see within 120 feet — the more spheres you make at once, the weaker each one is individually. Each sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> in a 30-foot radius and lasts as long as you <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">concentrate</a> on it (as if concentrating on a spell), up to 1 minute; you can move each one up to 30 feet as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, though never more than 120 feet from you. If a creature other than you comes within 5 feet of a sphere, the sphere discharges its lightning at that creature (DC 15 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dexterity\">Dexterity</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> for half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, with the amount scaling to how many spheres you made at once) and then winks out.</li></ul>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-telekinesis","title":"Ring of Telekinesis","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-telekinesis\">Telekinesis</a> from it at will, though you can target only objects that aren't currently being worn or carried by anyone.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-rings-legendary","title":"Legendary","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-djinni-summoning","title":"Ring of Djinni Summoning","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can speak its command word (action) to summon a specific djinni from the Elemental Plane of Air into an unoccupied space you choose within 120 feet. It stays as long as you <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">concentrate</a> on sustaining the summons (as if concentrating on a spell), up to 1 hour, or until it drops to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, at which point it returns home. While summoned, it's friendly toward you and your companions and follows any commands you give it regardless of language; left uncommanded, it defends itself but takes no other actions. Once it departs, you can't summon it again for 24 hours, and if it ever dies, the ring loses its magic for good.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-elemental-command","title":"Ring of Elemental Command","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring is bound to one of the four Elemental Planes — Air, Earth, Fire, or Water — chosen by the DM or determined randomly. While wearing it, you have Advantage on attack rolls against <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a> native to that plane, and they have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. As a Magic action, you can also target an elemental of that plane within 60 feet and force it to make a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 18) or take the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> condition until the start of your next turn; while it's charmed this way, you control its movement and its action on your turn. The ring separately has 5 charges for casting spells tied to its element, regaining 1d4+1 expended charges daily at dawn, with a save DC of 18 for any of them that call for one:</p><ul><li><strong>Air.</strong> You can speak and understand Auran. When you fall, you descend at only 60 feet per round and take no falling <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. You have Resistance to Lightning damage, and you have a flying <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed, including the ability to hover. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-chain-lightning\">Chain Lightning</a> (3 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wind-wall\">Wind Wall</a> (1 charge) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Earth.</strong> You can speak and understand Terran. Rubble, rocks, and dirt aren't <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a> for you, and you have Resistance to Acid damage. You can move through solid earth or rock as though it were Difficult Terrain, without disturbing the material you pass through; if you end your turn inside solid matter this way, you're shunted out to the nearest unoccupied space you last occupied. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stone-shape\">Stone Shape</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stoneskin\">Stoneskin</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-stone\">Wall of Stone</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Fire.</strong> You can speak and understand Ignan, and you're immune to Fire damage. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-burning-hands\">Burning Hands</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Water.</strong> You can speak and understand Aquan. You can stand on and move across liquid surfaces as though they were solid ground, you can breathe underwater, and you have a swimming Speed equal to your walking Speed.</li></ul><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This version exists as four separately named rings — Ring of Air Elemental Command, Ring of Earth Elemental Command, Ring of Fire Elemental Command, and Ring of Water Elemental Command — each granting a modest baseline benefit simply for wearing it, plus a much stronger set of benefits that unlock only once you help slay an elemental matching the ring's element while attuned to it. Each version also lets you expend 2 of the ring's 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dominate-monster\">Dominate Monster</a> (DC 17) on an elemental of its matching type; the ring regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn.</p><ul><li><strong>Air (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Auran, and when you fall, you descend at only 60 feet per round and take no falling damage. <strong>Air (after helping slay an air elemental).</strong> You gain Resistance to Lightning damage and a flying Speed equal to your walking Speed, including the ability to hover.</li><li><strong>Earth (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Terran, and rubble, rocks, and dirt aren't Difficult Terrain for you. <strong>Earth (after helping slay an earth elemental).</strong> You gain Resistance to Acid damage, and you can move through solid earth or rock as though it were Difficult Terrain, being shunted to the nearest unoccupied space you last occupied if you end your turn inside it; you can also cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stone-shape\">Stone Shape</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stoneskin\">Stoneskin</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-stone\">Wall of Stone</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Fire (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Ignan, and you have Resistance to Fire damage. <strong>Fire (after helping slay a fire elemental).</strong> Your Fire Resistance upgrades to immunity, and you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-burning-hands\">Burning Hands</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Water (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Aquan, and you can stand on and move across liquid surfaces as though they were solid ground. <strong>Water (after helping slay a water elemental).</strong> You can also breathe underwater and gain a swimming Speed equal to your walking Speed.</li></ul>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-invisibility","title":"Ring of Invisibility","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can take an action to turn invisible, taking anything you're wearing or carrying with you. You stay <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> until you remove the ring, until you attack or cast a spell, or until you spend a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to become visible again.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-spell-turning","title":"Ring of Spell Turning","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Advantage on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against spells. If you succeed on a save this way against a spell of level 7 or lower, that spell has no effect on you. If the spell also targeted only you, without creating any area of effect, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to hurl it back at its caster instead, who must then make their own saving throw against it, using their own spell save <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a>.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Advantage on saving throws against any spell that targets only you, without including you as part of a larger area of effect. If you roll a natural 20 on such a save and the spell is 7th level or lower, the spell has no effect on you at all, and instead targets its own caster — using that caster's slot level, spell save DC, spell attack bonus, and spellcasting ability, exactly as though they'd cast it at themselves.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-ring-of-three-wishes","title":"Ring of Three Wishes","html":"<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong></p><p>This ring has 3 charges. While wearing it, you can take an action and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> from it. Once its last charge is spent, the ring loses its magic and becomes an ordinary ring.</p>"}]}]},{"id":"magic-items-poisons","title":"Poisons","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-items-poisons-common","title":"Common","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-acid-tablets","title":"Acid Tablets","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Common</strong></p><p>Disguised as ordinary stomach tablets, these force a creature who swallows one to make a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d6 Acid <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and be unable to vomit for 30 seconds. At the start of each of its turns after that, the creature repeats the save; success lets it throw up and rid itself of the poison.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-basic-poison","title":"Basic Poison","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Common</strong></p><p>This vial of poison can coat one slashing or piercing weapon, or up to three pieces of ammunition; applying it takes an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> hit by the coated weapon or ammunition must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d4 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. Once applied, the poison stays potent for 1 minute before drying out.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-biza-s-breath","title":"Biza's Breath","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>A creature exposed to this poison must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1 minute. While poisoned this way, it must use its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to make a melee attack against a randomly determined creature within its reach, or do nothing on its turn if no other creature is in reach. It can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-dazzling-bomb","title":"Dazzling Bomb","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>Set off by a fuse or tripwire, this small bomb fills a 30-foot-diameter sphere with a highly irritating powder. Creatures caught in the powder must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be Stunned for 1 turn. <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-liquid-paranoia","title":"Liquid Paranoia","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Common</strong></p><p>A creature that ingests this poison gains the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition, with the source of its fear being the next <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> it sees within 5 minutes of drinking it. The creature must make a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>; on a failure, the fear lasts 1 hour, or half as long on a success.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-nausea-pellet","title":"Nausea Pellet","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>This black pellet can be thrown as an improvised weapon with a 20/40 range. On impact, it shatters into a fine powder filling a 5-foot square. Creatures in that square must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 30 seconds, repeating the save at the end of each of their turns. A poisoned creature can also use its action, or a Bonus Action while holding a Stomach Stopper, to throw up and end the poison early. Holding one's breath doesn't help, since the powder targets the nasal membranes; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-perfume-of-bewitching","title":"Perfume of Bewitching","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Common</strong></p><p>This tiny vial holds enough magic perfume for one use. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can apply it to yourself; for 1 hour afterward, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Charisma checks directed at <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoids</a> of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-challenge-rating\">challenge rating</a> 1 or lower, and those affected don't realize they've been magically influenced.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-poisons-uncommon","title":"Uncommon","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-angel-s-powder","title":"Angel's Powder","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This hyper-fine, bright white powder is blown into a target's face before dispersing harmlessly. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or, for 1 hour, perceive everyone around it as trusted friends, becoming extremely suggestible to non-aggressive persuasion and deception.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-assassin-s-blood","title":"Assassin's Blood","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 150 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must make a DC 10 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 6 (1d12) Poison damage and has the Poisoned condition for 24 hours. On a successful save, the creature takes half damage and isn't Poisoned.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-bane-berry-extract","title":"Bane Berry Extract","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>A creature that swallows this poison must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>. While poisoned this way, it has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Strength, Constitution, and Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> for 15 minutes. On a successful save, the target feels no effect at all.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-black-paste","title":"Black Paste","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact via clothing), Uncommon</strong></p><p>Designed to resemble leather or boot polish, this poison shines like new once applied to a piece of clothing. Wearing the treated garment for a total of 12 hours (not necessarily consecutive) forces a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the wearer takes 1d8 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. Unless the poisoned garment is removed, the saving throw repeats every 12 hours for the next 3 months.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-directed-delay","title":"Directed Delay","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This thick black liquid, viscous as concentrated molasses, is delivered through a wound or injection. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or suffer the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-slow\">Slow</a> spell, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns. On a successful save, its movement Speed is instead reduced by 5 feet for 3 turns.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-lava-paste","title":"Lava Paste","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This mundane-looking yellowish paste is applied to skin or clothing. The target must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d6 Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and become Vulnerable to fire damage for the next 12 hours; on a success, it takes half damage and avoids the vulnerability.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-malice","title":"Malice","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Blinded conditions for 1 hour.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-noxious-transpiration","title":"Noxious Transpiration","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This pale turquoise poison isn't dangerous to drink by itself, but starting 2 hours after ingestion, the drinker's sweat turns poisonous for 1 hour. Any contact with a patch of the drinker's skin roughly palm-sized or larger forces the toucher to succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d10+4 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>; a success avoids the damage entirely. Once a creature is exposed and takes no damage, it can't be affected by that dose again for 12 hours.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-pale-tincture","title":"Pale Tincture","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution saving throw or take 3 (1d6) Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition. The Poisoned creature repeats the save every 24 hours, taking another 3 (1d6) Poison damage on each failure; none of this damage can be healed by any means while the creature remains Poisoned. After seven successful saves, the creature is no longer Poisoned and can heal normally.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-philter-of-love","title":"Philter of Love","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>The next creature you see within 10 minutes of drinking this rose-hued, effervescent poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charms</a> you for 1 hour, and if it's a species and gender you're normally attracted to, you regard it as your true love for the duration.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-potion-of-poison","title":"Potion of Poison","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This concoction looks, smells, and tastes exactly like a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cure-wounds\">Potion of Healing</a> or other beneficial potion — only an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> spell reveals its true nature. Drinking it deals 3d6 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and forces a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition; while poisoned this way, the drinker takes another 3d6 Poison damage at the start of each of its turns and can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, with each successful save reducing the damage taken on subsequent turns by 1d6 until it reaches 0.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-serpent-venom","title":"Serpent Venom","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated giant poisonous snake. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or take 3d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-taratella-the-great-humiliator","title":"Taratella: The Great Humiliator","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This murky, muddy brown liquid forces the drinker to succeed on a DC 14 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> indefinitely. While poisoned this way, the target experiences vivid dreams and occasional hallucinations of onlookers laughing at it, taking 1d4+1 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> every 6 hours. On a successful save, the target is instead poisoned for 2 days, taking only 2 Psychic damage every 6 hours. The only known cure is to dance as poorly as possible for 1 hour in a town square during daylight.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-truth-serum","title":"Truth Serum","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 150 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition and be unable to speak a deliberate lie for 1 hour.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-poisons-rare","title":"Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-burnt-othur-fumes","title":"Burnt Othur Fumes","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 500 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) Poison damage, then repeat the saving throw at the start of each of its turns, taking 3 (1d6) Poison damage on each further failure. The poison ends after three successful saves.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-devil-s-powder","title":"Devil's Powder","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Rare</strong></p><p>This hyper-fine red powder is blown into a target's face before dispersing harmlessly. The target must succeed on a DC 18 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or perceive the world for 1 hour as a hellscape crawling with foul creatures, becoming extremely susceptible to intimidation, aggressive persuasion, and deception during that time. On a successful save, the target instead feels only mild paranoia and skittishness.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-dracula-s-essence","title":"Dracula's Essence","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>Kept as a small vial of what looks like fresh blood, this poison turns to a still, rust-colored liquid once opened. If drunk, or if it enters the bloodstream through a wound or injection, the target must succeed on a DC 18 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or immediately vomit up everything in its stomach and take 2d10 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, becoming unable to sleep; on a success, it instead vomits and takes 2d8 Poison damage. An hour later, the target becomes supremely sensitive to direct sunlight, taking 1d4 Fire damage for every minute it spends outside of shade while not wearing Muroosa Balm, and craves nothing but raw meat and blood (especially its own species') — trying to eat or drink anything else forces it to vomit and take 1d6 Poison damage. Each hour it goes without raw meat or blood, it gains 1 level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a>. These effects last 24 hours.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-drider-poison","title":"Drider Poison","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>Harvested directly from a drider rather than brewed, this venom forces a creature hit by a weapon or piece of ammunition coated in it to succeed on a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1 hour. If the save fails by 5 or more, the target is also <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-unconscious\">Unconscious</a> while poisoned this way. The target wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-essence-of-ether","title":"Essence of Ether","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 300 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 8 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-fire-plague","title":"Fire Plague","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Rare</strong></p><p>This rose-orange powder is baked into bread or pastry. Eating at least a quarter of the treated food forces a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the eater takes 1d6 Fire and 1d6 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, becomes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>, and develops necrotic patches across its skin. While poisoned this way, it suffers vivid hallucinations of death and dying, and can remake the saving throw each morning; a success ends all the effects.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-forgetfulness","title":"Forgetfulness","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Rare</strong></p><p>This fine, lavender powder forces anyone who breathes it in to succeed on a DC 14 Intelligence <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>. While poisoned this way, the target has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Intelligence <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> and checks, and must succeed on a DC 7 Intelligence check whenever it tries to recall anything that happened 4 or more weeks ago. It can repeat the saving throw at the start of every morning, ending the effect on a success.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-lolth-s-sting","title":"Lolth's Sting","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it also has the Unconscious condition while Poisoned this way. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Called \"Drow Poison.\" A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it also falls Unconscious for the same duration. The creature wakes up if it takes damage.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-magebane","title":"Magebane","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Rare</strong></p><p>Smelling of old boots despite its red-wine appearance, this poison grants the drinker the benefit of the Mage Slayer feat for 1 minute.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-magic-s-bane","title":"Magic's Bane","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>This clear, colorless poison holds a purple, cloudy sphere that darts through it. Once it enters a creature's bloodstream, the target must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or its ability to cast spells is disrupted for 1 minute, requiring a successful DC 10 Arcana check each time it tries to cast one anyway; a success avoids the disruption entirely. The saving throw can be repeated at the end of each of the target's turns.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-oil-of-taggit","title":"Oil of Taggit","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 24 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 24 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-thessaltoxin","title":"Thessaltoxin","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>First distilled from the blood of the artificer Thessalar, this poison forces a creature struck by it to succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take on a new form as if affected by the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> spell — a random beast, or a creature it's seen within the last 24 hours, chosen by the DM. The transformation lasts until the end of the target's next long rest, and isn't cured by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a>, though a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> spell restores the creature's true form.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-torpor","title":"Torpor","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 600 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition and have its Speed halved for 4d6 hours.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 600 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Incapacitated conditions for 4d6 hours.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-poisons-very-rare","title":"Very Rare","html":"","children":[{"id":"magic-item-armourer-s-blight","title":"Armourer's Blight","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This harmless-seeming, pale green liquid is designed to turn armor into a death trap. Poured, smeared, or thrown onto a piece of armor, it seeps into the metal and forces the wearer to succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> at the start of each of its turns or take 4d6 Lightning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>; a success reduces the damage to 4. The poison lasts for 10 years and can only be removed by heating the metal to at least 700°F/1300°F.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-black-thistle-poison","title":"Black Thistle Poison","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact, Injury, Ingested via fumes), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This jet-black poison, suspended with metallic cobalt mica-like powder, releases faint purple fumes for up to 30 minutes once its ampule is opened, filling a 10-foot cube. Applied to weapons or up to 10 pieces of ammunition, it stays active for 30 minutes (or 3 minutes on ammunition), continuing to give off the same fumes during that time.</p><p>Exposure to the fumes for more than 12 seconds forces a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the creature takes 4 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> for 30 seconds (2 Necrotic damage on a success); repeated brief exposure has no further effect for 12 hours. Exposure for 5 minutes or more in a day instead forces a DC 16 Constitution save, dealing 2d8 Necrotic damage and Blinding the creature for 5 days on a failure (half damage, no blindness on a success); a second cumulative 5 minutes of exposure deals 2d12 Necrotic damage and Blinds the creature permanently, curable only by regeneration magic or a potion, with no saving throw. Direct contact with the poison itself (blood or injection) is far more dangerous: a DC 18 Constitution save against 15+ minutes of fuming exposure, with a failure dealing 5d12 Necrotic damage and permanently Blinding and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafening</a> the creature, ruining its sense of smell and taste, and reducing its sense of touch by 80% for the rest of its life, with severe ongoing pain reducible only by regenerative magic or repeated Potions of Restoration; a success still deals 3d8 Necrotic damage and costs a sense (DM's choice) or reduces touch by 35% for 12 hours, curable the same way or with regenerative magic of a lower level.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-carrion-crawler-mucus","title":"Carrion Crawler Mucus","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated carrion crawler. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Paralyzed conditions for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns to end the effect early.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Called \"Crawler Mucus.\" A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-coup-de-poudre","title":"Coup de Poudre","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Made from herbs, powdered human bones, and animal poisons, this concoction is the first step in turning a living <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> into a loyal Revenant. If ingested, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 5d8 Necrotic and 5d8 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and fall into a death-like state at the stroke of midnight (half damage and no death-state on a success). A creature reduced to 0 hit points this way must be buried within 3 days and exhumed within 8 hours of burial, after which a 4-hour ritual binds its captured soul to the poisoner in a sealed jar; the body then reanimates as a Revenant that follows only verbal commands (given as a Bonus Action) in a language it understood in life, healing to full whenever it's midnight while the jar stays sealed and intact.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-deathsleep","title":"Deathsleep","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>A creature that ingests this poison must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 24 hours, appearing dead for the duration. Only a successful DC 20 Medicine check can determine that the creature is merely poisoned rather than truly dead.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-essence-of-rage","title":"Essence of Rage","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This muddy brown poison turns bright, violent red when agitated with more than the lightest touch. Drinking it grants the Barbarian class's Rage feature for 30 seconds. If instead introduced through a wound or injection, the target must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be forced into that same Rage for 30 seconds, compelled to attack the nearest target with melee attacks; on a success, it gains the benefit of Rage voluntarily for 60 seconds instead. A forced target can attempt another saving throw starting on its second turn under the effect, ending it on a success. This poison has no effect on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-medusa-s-vengeance","title":"Medusa's Vengeance","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This thick, grey poison is applied to weapons or ammunition, remaining active for 5 minutes on a weapon or 3 days on up to 20 pieces of ammunition (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected by it). The third time a coated weapon draws blood from the same target, that target must succeed on a DC 16 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or begin petrifying: it loses 5 feet of Speed at the start of each of its next 3 turns and, over the following 15 minutes, becomes increasingly sluggish before turning fully to stone. Once a target succeeds on the saving throw, it's immune to this poison for the next minute.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-midnight-tears","title":"Midnight Tears","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 1,500 GP per dose</p><p>A creature that ingests this poison suffers no effect until the stroke of midnight. If the poison hasn't been neutralized by then, the creature must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or take 9d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-night-hag-s-curse","title":"Night Hag's Curse","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Meant to torment rather than kill, this clear, lilac poison forces a target who ingests it or has it injected into their blood to succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a success, the target suffers vivid nightmares for a week, taking 4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> each morning upon waking. On a failure, the target's mind is permanently afflicted: it experiences night terrors that deal 2d10 Psychic damage upon waking each morning, and no longer automatically clears a level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> by completing a long rest — instead, the target rolls 1d100 each morning, restoring the level only on a 25 or lower, gaining a level instead on a 75 or higher, and seeing no change in between. The only cure is a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> spell of 6th level or higher, cast after the target drinks a Tea of Refreshment while it has no levels of Exhaustion.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-sandman-s-revenge","title":"Sandman's Revenge","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This yellowish, chunky powder is blown into a target's face. On contact, the target must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d10 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and gain 3 levels of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a>; on a success, it takes 4 Necrotic damage and gains only 1 level of Exhaustion. Holding one's breath doesn't help, since the powder targets the nasal membranes; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> are unaffected.</p>"},{"id":"magic-item-water-of-death","title":"Water of Death","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury, Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Looking, smelling, and tasting exactly like water, this poison defies even most magical and alchemical tests — only an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> spell cast at 7th level or higher, or 24 hours of detailed alchemical testing costing 300 gp, reveals what it truly is. Any contact with it forces a DC 20 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a> for 48 hours and too wracked with pain to move for 24 hours, its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Point</a> maximum permanently reduced by 2d12 before it takes 7d10 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> 12 hours later. On a successful save, its hit point maximum is still permanently reduced by 2d12, and it has blurred vision and muffled hearing for 24 hours. The lost hit point maximum can only be restored by healing after drinking a Potion of Vitality, or by a Greater Restoration or Regenerate spell cast at 8th level or higher.</p>"}]},{"id":"magic-items-poisons-legendary","title":"Legendary","html":"","children":[{"id":"equipment-purple-worm-poison","title":"Purple Worm Poison","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 2,000 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated purple worm. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 21 Constitution saving throw or take 10d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 2,000 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated purple worm. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution saving throw or take 12d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"},{"id":"equipment-wyvern-poison","title":"Wyvern Poison","html":"<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 1,200 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or take 7d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}]}]}]};
